NAME
       setfont - load a console font

SYNOPSIS
       setfont <font.psf|font.psfu>
       setfont <font.ttf|font.otf> [px]
       setfont -r
       setfont --once <font> [px]

DESCRIPTION
       Loads a console font. PSF and PSFU bitmap fonts are used at
       their own size; TrueType and OpenType fonts are rasterised with
       antialiasing at the pixel size given, 18 by default.

       Changing the font changes the character cell, so the console
       reflows and every full-screen program in the foreground is told
       about the new size.

OPTIONS
       -r, --reset      go back to the built-in font and forget the
                        saved one
       --once F [px]    load without saving as the default

FILES
       /etc/vconsole.conf   the saved font, applied at boot by init
       /usr/share/consolefonts, /usr/share/fonts

SEE ALSO
       csh(1)
